.TH QPATCH 1 "2026 May 14" "Qore 2.3" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qpatch \- command-line patch tool powered by the Qore Diff module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qpatch
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIpatch-file\fP
[\fItarget-file\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqpatch\fR applies a unified diff produced by \fBqdiff\fR(1) or any other
unified\-diff source to a target file using the Qore \fBDiff\fR module.
.PP
With no target file the patch's own file header is used.
With \fB\-d\fP / \fB\-\-dry\-run\fP the patch is only validated against the target
and no changes are written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Check whether the patch applies cleanly without modifying any files.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reverse
Reverse the patch (undo changes).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIFILE\fP
Write the patched result to \fIFILE\fP instead of overwriting the original.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show status messages.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Patch applied successfully (or dry-run passed).
.TP
.B 1
Patch failed (context mismatch).
.TP
.B 2
Error (missing file, invalid options).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qdiff (1),
.BR qore (1)
